{{Passive skill box|Supreme Ostentation}}
'''Supreme Ostentation''' is a {{il|Timeless Jewel}} only [[keystone passive skill]] which allows the player to ignore [[Attribute]] Requirements (on the gems and equipment) and removes inherent bonuses provided by those [[attribute]]s, thus making them irrelevant in most cases.

With the keystone allocated:

* [[Strength]] no longer provides maximum [[life]] and [[melee]] [[physical]] damage
* [[Dexterity]] no longer provides [[evasion]] and [[accuracy]]
* [[Intelligence]] no longer provides maximum [[mana]] and [[energy shield]]

This also effectively nullifies stats that directly modify attribute bonuses, such as {{psl|Iron Will}}, {{psl|Iron Grip}}, {{il|Iron Will Support}}, {{il|Iron Grip Support}}, or {{il|The Iron Fortress}}' {{c|mod|Strength's Damage Bonus instead grants 3% increased Melee Physical Damage per 10 Strength}}.

Supreme Ostentation does not disable other attribute-related effects, like {{il|Shaper's Touch}}, {{il|Mask of the Stitched Demon}}, {{psl|Magebane}}, {{psl|Solipsism}}.

This keystone's primary use is to equip high-attribute-requirement items such as {{il|Mjölner}}, {{il|page=Garb of the Ephemeral (Synthesised)}}, {{il|Cospri's Malice}}, {{il|Null's Inclination}}, {{il|Blunderbore}} {{il|Repentance}}, {{il|Zerphi's Heart}}, and {{il|Hand of the Lords}}. Builds making heavy use of [[tattoo]]s may also find this keystone useful, replacing all attribute travel passives.

==Location==
This keystone will replace (in-game wording [[Timeless Jewel#Conquered|conquered]]) any keystones within the radius of a {{il|Elegant Hubris}} jewel with modifier {{c|mod|Commissioned (2000-160000) coins to commemorate '''Caspiro'''}}.

